Windows-scRGB support for wlroots 0.20.2

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

The functional implementation below was written independently, then compared
with the existing Aqueous implementations. It follows the same factory,
scene-buffer flag and fixed 80 cd/m² normalization design; it is not a wholesale
backport of Aqueous's HDR stack. Documentation comments are adapted from:

* Aqueous 0006-color-management-v1-windows-hdr.patch, Zoey Bauer (2026-08-10)
  de683d2245e2c8d2f846add9d11fc342b2ddb534
  https://github.com/Seafoam-Labs/Aqueous/blob/de683d2245e2c8d2f846add9d11fc342b2ddb534/compositor/patches/wlroots/0006-color-management-v1-windows-hdr.patch
* Aqueous 0043-scene-buffer-windows-scrgb.patch, Zoey Bauer (2026-11-06),
  based on Christopher Snowhill (kode54)'s draft in Aqueous PR #127
  e52a8cddc93be2a5259de0240660fbc5d7ed85e4
  https://github.com/Seafoam-Labs/Aqueous/blob/e52a8cddc93be2a5259de0240660fbc5d7ed85e4/compositor/patches/wlroots/0043-scene-buffer-windows-scrgb.patch

Aqueous declares GPL-3.0-only; retain these attributions. The full GPL version 3
text: https://github.com/notdevblue/Dotfiles/blob/main/LICENSE
Local differences: a single
scRGB bool instead of the Windows-HDR kind enum, no unused snapshot getter,
no protocol-v3/BT.2100/output-metadata expansion, and explicit scanout rejection.
The 80/203 normalization composes with the preceding local sdr-white patch.

